{"audio": "1corinthians-03.opus", "duration_ms": 164416, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 3780, "text": "1 Corinthians, Chapter Three."}, {"start_ms": 5321, "end_ms": 11321, "text": "Brothers, I could not address you as spiritual, but as worldly—as infants in Christ."}, {"start_ms": 12021, "end_ms": 16562, "text": "I gave you milk, not solid food, for you were not yet ready for solid food."}, {"start_ms": 16922, "end_ms": 20422, "text": "In fact, you are still not ready, for you are still worldly."}, {"start_ms": 21082, "end_ms": 25062, "text": "For since there is jealousy and dissension among you, are you not worldly?"}, {"start_ms": 25662, "end_ms": 27463, "text": "Are you not walking in the way of man?"}, {"start_ms": 28143, "end_ms": 34403, "text": "For when one of you says, “I follow Paul,” and another, “I follow Apollos,” are you not mere men?"}, {"start_ms": 35383, "end_ms": 36484, "text": "What then is Apollos?"}, {"start_ms": 36884, "end_ms": 37724, "text": "And what is Paul?"}, {"start_ms": 38224, "end_ms": 42704, "text": "They are servants through whom you believed, as the Lord has assigned to each his role."}, {"start_ms": 43564, "end_ms": 47485, "text": "I planted the seed and Apollos watered it, but God made it grow."}, {"start_ms": 48465, "end_ms": 54045, "text": "So neither he who plants nor he who waters is anything, but only God, who makes things grow."}, {"start_ms": 54885, "end_ms": 61126, "text": "He who plants and he who waters are one in purpose, and each will be rewarded according to his own labor."}, {"start_ms": 61746, "end_ms": 66586, "text": "For we are God’s fellow workers; you are God’s field, God’s building."}, {"start_ms": 67567, "end_ms": 74147, "text": "By the grace God has given me, I laid a foundation as an expert builder, and someone else is building on it."}, {"start_ms": 74707, "end_ms": 77027, "text": "But each one must be careful how he builds."}, {"start_ms": 77528, "end_ms": 82988, "text": "For no one can lay a foundation other than the one already laid, which is Jesus Christ."}, {"start_ms": 83948, "end_ms": 94909, "text": "If anyone builds on this foundation using gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, or straw, his workmanship will be evident, because the Day will bring it to light."}, {"start_ms": 95509, "end_ms": 100270, "text": "It will be revealed with fire, and the fire will prove the quality of each man’s work."}, {"start_ms": 101110, "end_ms": 103890, "text": "If what he has built survives, he will receive a reward."}, {"start_ms": 104430, "end_ms": 106470, "text": "If it is burned up, he will suffer loss."}, {"start_ms": 106890, "end_ms": 110571, "text": "He himself will be saved, but only as if through the flames."}, {"start_ms": 111611, "end_ms": 116791, "text": "Do you not know that you yourselves are God’s temple, and that God’s Spirit dwells in you?"}, {"start_ms": 117231, "end_ms": 124592, "text": "If anyone destroys God’s temple, God will destroy him; for God’s temple is holy, and you are that temple."}, {"start_ms": 125392, "end_ms": 126772, "text": "Let no one deceive himself."}, {"start_ms": 127212, "end_ms": 133153, "text": "If any of you thinks he is wise in this age, he should become a fool, so that he may become wise."}, {"start_ms": 133773, "end_ms": 137153, "text": "For the wisdom of this world is foolishness in God’s sight."}, {"start_ms": 137853, "end_ms": 148814, "text": "As it is written: “He catches the wise in their craftiness.” And again, “The Lord knows that the thoughts of the wise are futile.” Therefore, stop boasting in men."}, {"start_ms": 149475, "end_ms": 156915, "text": "All things are yours, whether Paul or Apollos or Cephas or the world or life or death or the present or the future."}, {"start_ms": 157555, "end_ms": 163036, "text": "All of them belong to you, and you belong to Christ, and Christ belongs to God."}], "words": [{"t": "1", "s": 0, "e": 2420, "si": 0}, {"t": "Corinthians,", "s": 2420, "e": 3060, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter